<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shukri al-Quwatli</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1891">1891</a>–<a href="/years/1967">1967</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shukri al-Quwatli was a Syrian nationalist leader of the National Bloc who was elected president in 1943 under the French mandate. He led <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> to full independence when the last French troops left in April 1946. After defeat in the 1948 war with Israel he was overthrown in a military coup in 1949. Re-elected in 1955, he signed the union with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> in 1958.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shukri-al-quwatli.jpg" alt="Shukri al-Quwatli" width="320" height="415" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_Shukri_al-Quwatli_in_1943_(3x4_cropped).jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
